        "date": "2026-11-08T01:57:49Z"
      },
      "message": "fix: Fit to Models' cylinder is snug - the part's radius plus the allowance\n\nThe cylinder fit took its diameter from the padded footprint's diagonal,\nso a round part of radius R got a ~1.41 R bar, and since #130 every\nauto-fitted lathe setup roughs passes in air. It now takes the models'\nlargest horizontal distance from the fit's axis (a turned part's revolved\nmax radius) plus the margin: still containing every vertex, never larger\nthan before.\n\nFixes #230\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
